course: dictionary
lesson: 10104
title: A thinker is a person who thinks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A thinker is someone who thinks deeply and carefully, often about big or hard ideas. The word comes from think, with -er added to show a person who does it. Look at the words around it: «Each great thinker added something different; they did not all say the same thing.» Each thinker is a person, and each one adds ideas.
explain: Thinker can mean different kinds of thinker. «A quick thinker» is someone who thinks fast and solves problems quickly. «A creative thinker» comes up with new ideas. The words after thinker often tell you which kind is meant.
explain: Swap check: put "a person who thinks" in place of thinker. «Some thinkers say knowing is not the same as forcing» still makes sense, so thinkers means people who think carefully about the question.
fact: A thinker is a person who thinks deeply and carefully.
fact: «A quick thinker» means someone who thinks fast and solves problems quickly.
fact: «A creative thinker» means someone who comes up with new ideas.
fact: Teachers praise «critical thinkers», who ask questions and check reasons before they believe something.
fact: Great thinkers, such as Socrates, are studied in history and RE lessons.
exercise: «Each great thinker added something different; they did not all say the same thing.» In this sentence, what is a thinker? | A small animal that hops | *A person who thinks deeply and carefully | A kind of food | A type of tree
exercise: Ella says, «She is a quick thinker.» What does this mean? | *She thinks fast and solves problems quickly | She runs very fast | She writes stories quickly | She never thinks at all
exercise: What is the plural of thinker? | thinker | *thinkers | thinkes | thinkering
test: «Thinkers have found three big ways to ask what is right.» In this sentence, thinkers means | people who never ask questions | a type of cloud | a kind of tool | *people who have thought carefully about a question
test: Which phrase means someone who comes up with new ideas? | a deep thinker | a quick thinker | a free thinker | *a creative thinker
exam: «Whether God knowing the future leaves people free is a famous question in many religions.» Which word means a person who thinks about this question? | religions | question | future | *thinkers
